    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d919">

                <pb facs="0819" n="807" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg807"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/25076: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Henderson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Kuibyshev</hi> (<hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Moscow</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-10-26T15:00:00+03:00">October 26, 1942—3 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received October 26—1:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>933. Department’s 535, and 537 of October 24 arrived only today. I presented the
                    matter to Lozovski<anchor n="7" xml:id="d919-f1"/> this afternoon who hopes to
                    have a reply for me tomorrow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Henderson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d919-f1" n="7" xml:id="d919-f1-content">
                <p>S. A. Lozovsky, Assistant People’s Commissar for Foreign Affairs of the Soviet
                    Union.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
